Subject: [PATCH 11101/11171] [worktree-agent] Live-agent heartbeat, induce
 timing, ledger ingest, credit split (REQ-ARC-WMTE-7010..7013)

Baseline measured first, in docs/research-notes/arc-live-agent-baseline-four-axes-2026-09-04.md.
The classical path runs 272 actions in one second with the LLM off (one r11l run,
--budget 300), against 24,998 s for 2,077 actions in the post-fix r11l eval. The generator
is about 98 percent of a live eval. A single-game run still wrote nothing until it ended,
no row carried its wall clock, and no induction attempt carried its duration.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-7010 (scripts/arc_leaderboard_eval.py): ProgressWriter, an in-run heartbeat
file for the game in flight, rewritten on level-up, induce start and finish, new induction
attempt, and every 100 loop steps. Rows carry wall_s, started_at, finished_at,
generator_wall_s, induction_attempt_wall_s, progress_write_errors. The file uses
game_complete, never complete, so partial readers cannot mistake it for a banked game.
No write at construction, so the REQ-6850 tests that stub run_game are unchanged.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-7011 (arc_competition_agent.py): the routed path calls _induce_and_plan_timed,
a timed wrapper around _induce_and_plan, which keeps its name so the four existing source
pins on it still hold. Attempts carry started_at and wall_s on the normal and raising
paths. induction_progress_hook (default None) is told start and finish; a raising hook is
counted, never raised. Scored behaviour with no hook is unchanged.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-7012 (arc_supervisor_refinement.py): extract_rows accepts the eval's
{"per_game": [...]} shape and copies random_seed/policy/budget down before hashing, so a
partial and its final dedupe. Directory scans take *.json in arc_leaderboard_eval_runs.
EVAL_RUN_FIELDS_READ declared for the consumer-field lint. The ledger was re-ingested:
9 receipts / 6 redirects became 14 / 31, two arms reached the floor of 10, and the tool
now emits a new-arm specification from the r11l cell. Nothing was removed from it.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-7013 (arc_trajectory_supervisor.py): each credited redirect carries
co_credited_count; the receipt gains an additive arm_credit key (helped_sole,
helped_share); shadow mode renames it would_have_arm_credit; the refinement report shows
sole and share next to the pooled helped. arm_outcomes keeps its exact 6640 shape and
the decision rules are unchanged.

Rejected: putting the credit split inside arm_outcomes (existing tests assert exact
equality on it); a control-arm estimator (no window-120 shadow receipt with a firing
exists yet); any GPU run (GPU 1 was allocated to another eval at 21:23Z).

Adversarial review (read-only sub-agent) applied before this commit: EVAL_RUN_FIELDS_READ
now names the document-level fields (per_game, random_seed, policy, budget); the eval-runs
scan and scripts/eval_run_consumer_field_lint.py both skip *.progress.json heartbeats (one
lint test added); helped_share accumulates unrounded and rounds once at emit; the note
labels the 24,998 s as inferred and names the scratch scores file. Not changed: the ledger
`source` of a partial file stays as written (the entry holds the evidence itself, REQ-6720
rule 2); a level-up on a period boundary writes twice, which only inflates `writes`.

Proof: 27 new tests in four files; 11 mutations RED with byte-identical restores, scored
only after a green unmutated baseline. The first proof pass produced 11 void REDs because
"-p no:xdist" conflicts with the project addopts; the baseline gate exists because of it.
Two policy-constructing test files carry memory_watchdog_skip (+549 MB on a fresh worker).

